-- status  : Open
-- author  : @mikedeng1
-- created : 2026-10-07T20:07:39.813992+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/e6fcd090-268d-46c7-9c40-d85bd32dde95
-- title:
--   Theorem 4, p. 11 — under (G₂dis), (G₃dis), (IPAHD) satisfies f(x_k) − min f = O(1/δ_k) and Σ_k δ_kβ_{k+1}‖∇f(x_{k+1})‖² < +∞
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal H$ be a real Hilbert space and $f:\mathcal H\to\mathbb R$ a convex function of class $\mathcal C^1$ that attains its minimum at some $x^\star$. Let $\alpha\ge1$, let $h>0$ be the step size and $s=h^2$, and let $(\beta_k)_{k\in\mathbb N}$, $(b_k)_{k\in\mathbb N}$ be non-negative sequences. Set
--   $$\delta_k:=h\big(b_khk-\beta_{k+1}-k(\beta_{k+1}-\beta_k)\big)(k+1) \tag{9}$$
--   and suppose that, for some $k_0\ge1$ and every $k\ge k_0$, the growth conditions hold:
--   $$(\mathcal G_2^{\rm dis})\quad b_khk-\beta_{k+1}-k(\beta_{k+1}-\beta_k)>0,\qquad(\mathcal G_3^{\rm dis})\quad \delta_{k+1}-\delta_k\le(\alpha-1)\frac{\delta_k}{k+1}.$$
--   Let $(x_k)_{k\in\mathbb N}$ be generated by the **Inertial Proximal Algorithm with Hessian Damping** (IPAHD): for $k\ge1$, with $\mu_k=\frac{k}{k+\alpha}(\beta_k\sqrt s+sb_k)$,
--   $$y_k=x_k+\Big(1-\frac{\alpha}{k+\alpha}\Big)(x_k-x_{k-1})+\beta_k\sqrt s\Big(1-\frac{\alpha}{k+\alpha}\Big)\nabla f(x_k),\qquad x_{k+1}=\mathrm{prox}_{\mu_kf}(y_k).$$
--   Then:
--   1. $\delta_k>0$ for every $k\ge k_0$;
--   2. $f(x_k)-\min_{\mathcal H}f=\mathcal O(1/\delta_k)$ as $k\to+\infty$;
--   3. $\displaystyle\sum_k\delta_k\beta_{k+1}\|\nabla f(x_{k+1})\|^2<+\infty$.
--
--   For $k\ge1$, $1/\delta_k=h^{-1}\cdot\frac{1}{k(k+1)\left(b_kh-\frac{\beta_{k+1}}{k}-(\beta_{k+1}-\beta_k)\right)}$, so (2) is also the paper's second form $\mathcal O\big(1/(k(k+1)(b_kh-\beta_{k+1}/k-(\beta_{k+1}-\beta_k)))\big)$. With $\beta_k\equiv\beta>0$ and $b_k=1+\beta/(hk)$, for instance, $\delta_k=h^2(k+1)k$ and the rate is $\mathcal O(1/k^2)$.
--
--   The theorem transfers the accelerated rates of the continuous dynamic with Hessian-driven damping to an implicit (proximal) algorithm, for general varying damping sequences.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The growth conditions are assumed for every $k\ge k_0$ with $k_0\ge1$ a parameter: at $k=0$, $(\mathcal G_2^{\rm dis})$ reads $-\beta_1>0$, which no non-negative sequence satisfies, so a reading "for all $k\in\mathbb N$" would make the theorem vacuous; the paper's own examples state them "for all $k\ge\dots$". Accordingly the positivity of $\delta_k$ is concluded for $k\ge k_0$. The hypotheses $h>0$ and $\beta_k,b_k\ge0$ are not printed in the theorem but are implicit (positive step size; $\mu_k\ge0$; the proof uses $\beta_{k+1}\ge0$); they are the discrete analogue of the standing hypothesis (H). $\min f$ is $f(x^\star)$ for a point $x^\star$ with $f(x^\star)\le f(y)$ for all $y$ ((H): $\mathrm{argmin} f\neq\emptyset$). The run is required to satisfy the proximal step for $k\ge1$, with $x_0,x_1$ free. $\mathcal O$ is Mathlib's `=O[atTop]`; the summability is `Summable` in $\mathbb R$.
-- source:
--   Attouch, Chbani, Fadili, Riahi, First-order optimization algorithms via inertial systems with Hessian driven damping, arXiv:1907.10536v2, p. 11, Theorem 4, (9), (IPAHD)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GoldenRatioVI_Shared_IsProxPoint
import Definitions.Def_HessianDamping_IPAHD_Setting

namespace HessianDamping.IPAHD

/-- Theorem 4, p. 11. -/
theorem theorem_4
    {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] [CompleteSpace H]
    (f : H → ℝ) (hfconv : ConvexOn ℝ Set.univ f) (hfC1 : ContDiff ℝ 1 f)
    (xstar : H) (hxstar : ∀ y, f xstar ≤ f y)
    (α : ℝ) (hα : 1 ≤ α)
    (h s : ℝ) (hh : 0 < h) (hs : s = h ^ 2)
    (β b : ℕ → ℝ) (hβ : ∀ k, 0 ≤ β k) (hb : ∀ k, 0 ≤ b k)
    (x : ℕ → H) (hx : IsIPAHDRun f α s β b x)
    (k₀ : ℕ) (hk₀ : 1 ≤ k₀)
    (hG2 : ∀ k : ℕ, k₀ ≤ k → 0 < b k * h * k - β (k + 1) - k * (β (k + 1) - β k))
    (hG3 : ∀ k : ℕ, k₀ ≤ k →
      deltaK h β b (k + 1) - deltaK h β b k ≤ (α - 1) * deltaK h β b k / ((k : ℝ) + 1)) :
    (∀ k : ℕ, k₀ ≤ k → 0 < deltaK h β b k) ∧
    (fun k : ℕ => f (x k) - f xstar) =O[Filter.atTop] (fun k : ℕ => 1 / deltaK h β b k) ∧
    Summable (fun k : ℕ => deltaK h β b k * β (k + 1) * ‖gradient f (x (k + 1))‖ ^ 2) := by sorry

end HessianDamping.IPAHD
